                        "entry_id": "43738d70-daba-3f27-889f-24a23f225ec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "傑出的，卓越的；優越的"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5f2c603-4e83-49a5-a0d4-da38ea95716b",
                                "sense_id": "6c7603cb-a7d7-30d1-81c4-08f338e93dbf",
                                "text": "so far was beauty adored amongst them, that no man was thought fit to reign that was not in all parts complete and supereminent.",
                                "translation": "他们极其崇拜美貌，所以除非一个人在各方面都完美无缺、出类拔萃，否则就认为他不适合统治。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1cf39fc-3f04-4825-91e6-e8ab3908b732",
                                "sense_id": "6c7603cb-a7d7-30d1-81c4-08f338e93dbf",
                                "text": "But these two ideas: first, the supereminent claims of the State above the claims of any of the lesser groups included within it, the right of the State to crush out family affection and individual warfare in order to its own perpetuation,—as in the case of Brutus sentencing his own son, of Coriolanus, of the Horatii, etc.; and, secondly, the right of all who are willing to conform to the requirements of the State to be included within the domain of citizenship.",
                                "translation": "但是，有两个观念：第一，国家享有高于它其中任何较小群体的至高权利，国家有权压制家庭间的感情和个人间的冲突以维持其自身统治，就像布鲁图斯判处自己儿子死刑、科利奥兰纳斯判处赫拉斯兄弟死刑等等；第二，所有愿意遵守国家要求的人都有权成为公民。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
